# CorpusCriste — Deploy

## Routes

1. Next.js App Router routes = folder structure under `app/`
2. Navbar options = `specs/routes.json` (use `parent` for dropdown children)
3. **Never** configure Vercel-only routes without matching `app/` and `specs/routes.json`

## New nested route

Create `app/{section}/{slug}/page.tsx` and register in specs.

## Legacy redirects (vercel.json)

```json
{
  "redirects": [
    { "source": "/slug-antigo", "destination": "/secao/novo-slug", "permanent": true }
  ]
}
```

When renaming public URLs, add a permanent redirect.

## Deploy flow

Push to GitHub → Vercel Git integration detects Next.js → `npm run build`

- **No GitHub Actions.** The account is at the free-tier limit; do not add `.github/workflows/`. Run `npm run test:specs`, `npm run build` and `CI=1 npm run test:e2e` locally before pushing.
- `main` = production (https://www.grupodeuseamor.com.br).
- `v2` = branch of the v2 snapshots (`2.0.0-snapshot` … `2.6.x-snapshot`) → automatic **Preview Deployment** (branch URL). Review there before tagging `v2.N.0-snapshot` (or patch `v2.N.x-snapshot`).
- Official release 2.7.0: merge `v2` → `main`, tag `v2.7.0`, GitHub Release Latest. Rollback: Vercel *Instant Rollback* to the last 1.1.0 deployment and/or revert the merge (code preserved in release `v1.1.0`).
- v2 does **not** rename public URLs, so no new redirects are needed.

Static assets (`public/`, `_next/static/`) are cached automatically by Vercel/Next.js. Do not add custom `headers` regex patterns in `vercel.json` — path-to-regexp rejects patterns like `/(.*\\.(png|jpg))`.
